   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Difference between Constituency Parsing and Dependency Parsing\n",
    "\n",
    "**Constituency Parsing (NLTK):**\n",
    "- Divides the sentence into phrases (constituents) hierarchically\n",
    "- Generates a tree where phrases are grouped at different levels\n",
    "- Example: \"(NP the cat) (VP (V saw) (NP the dog))\"\n",
    "- Focus: **phrase structure**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dependency Parsing (spaCy):**\n",
    "- Identifies relationships between individual words\n",
    "- Each word has a \"head\" (dependent word)\n",
    "- Example: \"cat\" depends on \"saw\" (nsubj), \"dog\" depends on \"saw\" (dobj)\n",
    "- Focus: **relationships between words**\n"
   ]
  },
