   "source": [
    "### NLTK vs spaCy Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "**KEY DIFFERENCES:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Output Structure:**\n",
    "   - NLTK: Hierarchical tree of constituents (Tree object)\n",
    "   - spaCy: Linear relationships between tokens (dependency arcs)\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Information Captured:**\n",
    "   - NLTK: Groups words into phrases (NP, VP, PP, etc.)\n",
    "   - spaCy: Shows grammatical relationships (nsubj, dobj, amod, etc.)\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Visualization:**\n",
    "   - NLTK: Tree with hierarchical structure\n",
    "   - spaCy: Directed graph with dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Accuracy:**\n",
    "   - NLTK: Depends on the RegExp Grammar you define\n",
    "   - spaCy: Uses trained ML models (more accurate but less controllable)\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Use Cases:**\n",
    "   - NLTK: Better for structural phrase analysis\n",
    "   - spaCy: Better for extracting grammatical relationships and dependencies\n"
   ]
  },
